From 14d6cb3bdebdc226bf264dc27c8e6dbfa7267491 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Miller Bath <millerzbath@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:04:40 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat: cancel a transfer to a remote terminal, or all of
 them
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Each queued or sending row has a ×, and the header has Cancel all. A
queued item never starts; the sending one's hc put is killed, its path is
not pasted, and what part of it arrived (the path hc's progress named) is
removed there with hc exec rm -rf. The header counts cancelled items.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
